      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for squid",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for squid fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-32748: denial of service in ICP Request handling (bsc#1260453).\n- CVE-2026-33515: out of bounds read in ICP message handling (bsc#1260454).\n- CVE-2026-33526: denial of service in ICP Request handling (bsc#1260452).\n- CVE-2026-47729: out-of-bounds read attack against the ftp gateway due to a improper validation of syntactic\n  correctness of input (bsc#1268272).\n- CVE-2026-50012: Improper Input Validation bug (bsc#1268320).\n\nChanges for squid:\n\nUpdate to 6.14:\n\n  - Do not leak HttpReply when checking http_reply_access (bsc#1237027)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
